+    // Dispatch-rate instrumentation (2026-08-20). The worker burns 77% of a
+    // core with zero profile samples in guest code, and removing the poll
+    // sleep, the lock churn and a per-slice allocation each changed nothing -
+    // so the question is whether this loop is turning over far faster than the
+    // audio hardware consumes buffers. At 48 kHz with the usual frame size the
+    // healthy rate is a couple of hundred dispatches a second.
+    static std::atomic<uint64_t> waits{0}, successes{0}, timeouts{0}, dispatches{0};
